limactl-start.log
=================

The transcript internal/narrate is tested against. Its whole value is
provenance: patterns written from memory, tested against lines written from
the same memory, prove nothing about what lima actually prints.

THIS COPY IS RECONSTRUCTED, NOT CAPTURED. It was written from lima's message
shapes while ptrbox was being built on Linux against a faked limactl, because
no Mac was available to run a real `limactl start` on. Replace it at the first
`make smoke`:

    limactl start --name scratch ~/.lima/_generated/scratch.yaml 2>&1 \
      | tee internal/narrate/testdata/limactl-start.log

Then run `make test` and read what changed. Lines the translator does not
recognise are shown verbatim rather than dropped, so a mismatch surfaces as
untranslated output rather than as a missing step - but untranslated output is
exactly what this file exists to prevent.

Not a .md file on purpose: this repo gitignores *.md, and a note about a
fixture's trustworthiness is worth less than nothing if it is untracked.

limafake replays this file when a test asks it to, so the command-level tests
and the translator's own tests run on identical bytes.
